  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 28f310e05cc019a48855581da30b411e, type: 3}
  m_Name: PancitPusitHistory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - text: Our next dish comes from the coastal food traditions of Cavite! Get ready
      for Pancit Pusit, a noodle dish with a very distinctive look.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Let me tell you the history and origin of pancit pusit.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Cavite Pancit Pusit is associated with Cavite City's Chabacano food culture.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Its name, Pancit Choko en Su Tinta, refers to noodles cooked with squid
      and its ink, combining Chinese-influenced noodle traditions with locally available
      seafood.
    characterSprite: {fileID: 0}
  - text: The squid ink gives the dish its signature dark color, while garlic, onions,
      and seasonings add flavor.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: Though its exact origins are not fully documented, it remains a distinctive
      part of Cavite's culinary heritage.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -511706578061346315, guid: ae71825725b21a3459805439433622ee, type: 3}
  - text: Did you know?
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: Those dark noodles get their color from squid ink.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: The name Choko en Su Tinta also reflects the influence of Chabacano, a
      language shaped by Spanish and local influences.
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
  - text: Let's give these noodles their signature color and bring this coastal specialty
      to life!
    characterSprite: {fileID: -8056027616224820867, guid: 783feefcd5809a142b7b39ffbbe1c917, type: 3}
